{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q014_paper_example_reclassification_pa1492","answer":"The relationship changed from "not in the same fold" in SCOP 1.69 to "same SCOPe superfamily, but still different families" in the current SCOPe release. SCOPe reports the current public release as 2.08, with latest periodic update 2.08-2026-08-16. In SCOP 1.69, the PA1492 domains from PDB 1t1j were d1t1ja_ and d1t1jb_, both classified as c.137.1.1: class c, Alpha and beta proteins (a/b); fold c.137, Hypothetical protein PA1492; superfamily c.137.1, Hypothetical protein PA1492; family c.137.1.1, Hypothetical protein PA1492. In that same release, nucleoside 2-deoxyribosyltransferase from PDB 1f8y was already d1f8ya_/d1f8yb_ in c.23.14.1: class c; fold c.23, Flavodoxin-like; superfamily c.23.14, N-deoxyribosyltransferase; family c.23.14.1, N-deoxyribosyltransferase. Thus in release 1.69, 1t1j and 1f8y shared only the very broad alpha/beta class, not a fold, superfamily, or family, and SCOP 1.69 was treating PA1492 as its own fold.

In current SCOPe 2.08, the PA1492 protein parts of 1t1j are d1t1ja1 and d1t1jb1, residues A:1-118 and B:1-118, with the same domain SUNIDs 106249 and 106250 but moved to c.23.14.2. Their lineage is class c, Alpha and beta proteins (a/b); fold c.23, Flavodoxin-like; superfamily c.23.14, renamed N-(deoxy)ribosyltransferase-like; family c.23.14.2, Hypothetical protein PA1492. The 1f8y chains remain in c.23.14.1 under the same c.23.14 superfamily. So Andreeva et al.'s PA1492 example is a reclassification/merge of the PA1492 fold c.137 into the Flavodoxin-like fold c.23 and specifically into the same N-(deoxy)ribosyltransferase-like superfamily as 1f8y, while preserving PA1492 as a separate family from the enzymatic N-deoxyribosyltransferase family.

The evolutionary-strength limit is important: after the SCOPe reclassification, SCOPe treats PA1492 and 1f8y as superfamily-level homologs, which is weaker than same-family membership; before the reclassification, SCOP 1.69 made no such fold- or superfamily-level grouping. The current placement can justify using 1f8y as a remote structural template or structural analogue for the PA1492 core, but it should not be used to transfer the specific nucleoside 2-deoxyribosyltransferase family assignment or enzymatic function to PA1492. In 2.08, 1t1j also has short l.1.1.1 synthetic N-terminal tag entries, d1t1ja2 and d1t1jb2; those artifact/tag domains are not the PA1492 core and should not be selected as representatives of the c.23.14.2 family.","evidence_used":["/api/v1/","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1t1j","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1f8y","/api/v1/releases/1.69/pdb/1t1j","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1t1j/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1f8y/domains","/api/v1/releases/1.69/pdb/1t1j/domains","/api/v1/releases/1.69/pdb/1f8y/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1t1ja1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1f8ya_","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sids/d1t1ja_","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sids/d1f8ya_","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110463","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52312","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/110463","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/52312","/api/v1/openapi.yaml","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110463/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/31395/parents","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/106249/parents","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/31395/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/282689/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/106249/annotations","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/106249/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52309/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110461/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52310/homology"]}]}
